+## Experimental negative-case preparation
+
+During criteria preparation, write a concise project-specific negative-case matrix for the applicable frozen requirements. Include relevant invalid types and values, boundary values, missing resources or unknown entry points, and the guarantee that rejected or failed writes do not mutate valid state. Each applicable row identifies the requirement, expected observable result, and planned check; mark irrelevant classes with a reason. The matrix maps the existing acceptance bar and does not add or weaken product requirements.
+
+The independent reviewer challenges matrix coverage during the existing design challenge before implementation. Before the final review handoff, the lead executes a concrete check for each applicable class and preserves its actual command/action and observed result. These preparation and handoff artifacts do not replace independent behavior checks, exact-source review, fresh evidence or any acceptance gate. Treat this as an experimental practice until matched trials show useful evidence; unchanged ownership and workflow transitions still apply.
 
